{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The 'refuted if' condition is tautological and self-immunizing. The claimed contradiction is that installation does not uniformly constrain registry targets (evidenced by 3-of-26 success rate). The proposed refutation condition—'if the same installation ritual reproduces the 3-of-26 ratio on a larger, multi-author repository'—would CONFIRM rather than refute the claim. If a larger repository also shows only 3-of-26 targets failing first, this provides additional evidence that installation fails to uniformly constrain targets (since 23-of-26 still pass), strengthening rather than undermining the original assertion. A genuine refutation would require showing that installation DOES uniformly constrain targets (e.g., a high success rate like 26-of-26 or 25-of-26 on a comparable repository), not reproducing the same failure pattern.","counterexample":["If a larger repository also shows 3/26 success, this confirms the original 3/26 observation rather than contradicting it.","To refute 'not uniformly constraining', evidence of uniform constraint (e.g., 26/26 or 25/26 success) is required, not replication of the same sparse success rate."],"premise":"Reproducing the same 3-of-26 failure ratio would refute the claim that installation does not uniformly constrain targets","premise_evidence":[{"block":"007dca563e8d","quote":"it is refuted if the same installation ritual reproduces the 3-of-26 ratio on a larger, multi-author repository"}],"target":"aa69ba5ad78a024aef4eba64077b5707da5fe92e797c41fd3409ff99865a08cc"}]}